course: dictionary
lesson: 9780
title: Surprise: one word, three jobs
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word surprise can be a thing, a feeling, or an action. The words around it show you which one it is. «A surprise can make you gasp.» Here a surprise is a thing, something that happened without warning.
explain: «Her surprise was huge when she opened the door.» Here surprise is the feeling you have when something unexpected happens. The clue is "was huge", which describes a feeling.
explain: «The news will surprise everyone.» Here surprise is a verb: it means to do something people did not expect. Check it by swapping in "make everyone feel surprised". The sentence still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Other forms help too. Surprised describes how a person feels, and surprising describes the thing that causes the feeling. «The surprising result made the scientists check again» means the result was one nobody had predicted.
fact: A surprise is something you did not expect, such as a present or a sudden event.
fact: Surprise is also the feeling you have when something unexpected happens.
fact: To surprise someone means to do something they did not expect, often to make them happy.
fact: «A good secret, like a surprise party or a hidden present, ends happily and nobody gets hurt.»
fact: Useful phrases: to my surprise, take someone by surprise, what a surprise.
exercise: «The children planned a surprise party for Grandma.» What is a surprise party? | A party just for the dog | A party held every single year | A party that cancels at the last minute | *A party Grandma does not know about until it starts
exercise: Jayden writes, «To my surprise, the test was easy.» What does "to my surprise" tell us? | Jayden was sure the test would be easy | The test was very long | *Jayden had not expected the test to be easy | Jayden was sad about the test
exercise: «Some surprises hide in the kitchen: a potato is a swollen stem, not a root.» What does surprise mean here? | A party with food | *Something you would not expect to be true | A kind of potato | A loud noise in the kitchen
test: «A surprising result is one you did not predict, which makes you check and think again.» What does surprising mean? | Something you predicted perfectly | Something that is always true | *Something you did not predict | Something very loud
test: Which word describes a person who feels amazed when a present arrives unexpectedly? | Surprising | *Surprised | Surprise party | Surprises
exam: Why is a surprise party kept secret? | *So the guest is caught off guard and happy when it starts | So the food gets cold | So the party is never held | So nobody can bring a present
